frica has the festive season covered with a packed line-up of live sport, on channels across the continent and Disney+ in SA.","published":"2026-11-23T08:34:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50571229/sport-espn-africa-festive-watch-dstv-disney+","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"49ers' Brock Purdy beats Vikings blitz, hears 'MVP' chants in Mexico City","description":"Quarterback Brock Purdy heard \"MVP\" chants in Mexico City and continued to earn praise from his teammates as he led the 49ers to a statement victory against the top-ranked Vikings defense on Sunday night","published":"2026-11-23T07:58:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50571034/49ers-brock-purdy-beats-vikings-blitz-hears-mvp-chants-mexico-city","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Nick Wagoner","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NFL Week 11: Big takeaways, questions and fantasy spin from Sunday's games","description":"Our NFL Nation reporters react to all the action, answering the biggest questions coming out of each Sunday game. Here's what we learned from Week 11.","published":"2026-11-23T05:53:02.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50563342/week-11-sunday-games-takeaways-questions-2026","type":"Story","byline":"NFL Nation","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Fantasy buzz: Week 11's leading fantasy scorers through \"Sunday Night Football\"","description":"A closer look at the top 10 fantasy scorers in Week 11, including Cowboys QB Dak Prescott and Broncos RB Jonah Coleman.","published":"2026-11-23T04:53:26.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/fantasy/football/story/_/id/40699880/fantasy-football-injuries-position-battles-nfl-news-analysis","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN Fantasy","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tracking Jaguars CB/WR Travis Hunter's 2026 season: Snaps on offense, defense","description":"Every week, we will look at how many snaps the two-way corner/receiver plays on offense and defense. Is there a trend in his usage?","published":"2026-11-23T04:56:42.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50043976/jacksonville-jaguars-travis-hunter-stats-snaps-tracker","type":"Story","byline":"Michael DiRocco","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 11 NFL highlights: Best plays, moments, touchdowns, more","description":"Check here for all of the top moments, TDs and analysis from games at the Broncos, Jets, Cowboys, Eagles and more.","published":"2026-11-23T04:50:41.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50562956/week-11-highlights-sunday-best-plays-touchdowns-2026","type":"Story","byline":"NFL Nation","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Jacob Saylors","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacob_Saylors","description":"American football player (born 2000)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:21Z","intro":"Jacob Saylors (born March 8, 2000) is an American professional football kick returner and running back for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the East Tennessee State Buccaneers and was signed by the Cincinnati Bengals as an undrafted free agent following the 2023 NFL Draft. With the St. Louis Battlehawks, Saylors was named to the All-UFL team in 2024 and 2025.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Saylors played college football at East Tennessee State, where he rushed for 3,861 yards, and 33 touchdowns.\n\nSTATISTICS"},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"CINCINNATI BENGALS\nAfter going undrafted in the 2023 NFL draft, Saylors signed with the Cincinnati Bengals on April 30, 2023. He was waived by the Bengals on August 29.\n\nATLANTA FALCONS\nOn October 18, 2023, Saylors was signed to the Atlanta Falcons' practice squad. He was waived on January 2, 2024, with an injury settlement.\n\nST. LOUIS BATTLEHAWKS (FIRST STINT)\nOn February 5, 2024, Saylors signed with the St. Louis Battlehawks of the United Football League (UFL). He led the league in rushing yards, and was named to the All-UFL team.\n\nNEW YORK GIANTS\nOn June 18, 2024. Saylors signed with the New York Giants. He was waived by the Giants on August 12.\n\nCLEVELAND BROWNS\nOn August 22, 2024, Saylors signed with the Cleveland Browns, but was waived later that week.\n\nST. LOUIS BATTLEHAWKS (SECOND STINT)\nOn November 5, 2024, Saylors re-signed with the Battlehawks.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn July 29, 2025, Saylors signed with the Detroit Lions. He was waived on August 26 as part of final roster cuts, and re-signed to the practice squad. He was promoted to the active roster on September 6. In his first NFL regular season game, Saylors primarily played as a return specialist, returning four kickoffs for a total of 92 yards.\nOn January 5, 2026, the Lions signed Saylors to a one-year contract extension."}],"wikidataId":"Q134625884","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-01-05","text":"Signed OLs Devin Cochran and Mason Miller, WRs Malik Cunningham and Jackson Meeks, DE Ahmed Hassanein, TE Zach Horton, RB Jabari Small, DL Chris Smith and S Loren Strickland to reserve/futures contracts. Re-signed OL Michael Niese, RB Jacob Saylors and CB Nick Whiteside."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4383429","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/S/SaylJa00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/jacob-saylors/87559","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/jacob-saylors/11476","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacob_Saylors"},"insights":["2026 cap number of $1.0M is the 45th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Entered the league in 2023 as an undrafted free agent."]}